From a9d622500023531e9d04b856f1b2a64c37ac88a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:09:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] Concurrent mark: prepare the mark bits and start the
 epoch without a pause

The start pause only lists the roots, stacks and thread locals now (about 40
us at 2 GiB, was 1 to 3 ms). The mark bits are prepared with the program
running, in short steps like the sweep, after the epoch has started so that
whatever the program creates meanwhile is born and needs none.

Four races this change opened, each found by a test (mark_race, alloc with 8
threads under the verifier, the Phobos stress):

- the tracker is armed before the epoch starts, or a born object written in
  between is never reported (mark_race: hundreds of damaged nodes);
- the epoch starts and the bins are emptied as one step with every bin locked,
  because in either order a slab slips in between and the heap is corrupted;
- a slab made before the epoch that reaches a bin after it is tagged born;
- the set of arenas to lock is taken once: an arena initialized meanwhile made
  us unlock a mutex we had not locked (a rare hang or Lock not held).

Gate with SYMGC_CONCURRENT_MARK=1: worst frame 512 MiB 10.7 -> 1.7 ms, 2 GiB
31.0 -> 1.75 ms.
